  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA distributed value fell 3.3% over 30D:</strong> On-chain RWA distributed value at $15.64B (3.3% lower over 30D) hints that tokenized asset growth paused or reversed\u2014more consistent with risk-off allocation or redemptions than a pure news cycle. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/business/2026-08-24-bernstein-says-circles-growth-cycle-can-continue-without-the-clarity-act-sees-59-upside-412573\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bernstein says Circle\u2019s growth cycle can continue without the Clarity Act, sees 59% upside</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitmine-eth-holdings-5-percent-ether-price-breakout?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bitmine extends 14-month ETH buying pace as Ether breaks above $2.5K</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Tokenized T-bill supply is still expanding through new products:</strong> That usually shows up first as new issuer and product supply, then as higher distributed value and denser collateral-style use across networks and platforms. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/08/24/strategy-raises-usd2-billion-through-mstr-sales-and-creates-new-usd-cash-pool\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Strategy raises $2 billion through MSTR sales and creates new USD Cash pool</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/regulation/2026-08-25-blockchain-association-backs-genius-act-412668\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Blockchain Association backs Treasury\u2019s proposed GENIUS Act rules for stablecoin issuers</a> (The Block).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
